   "id": 518793,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Calculate and interpret the effective annual yield on a deposit earning 2.5% compounded daily.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Effective annual yield is <span data-math=\"Y = {\\left({1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)^n} - 1\"></span> where <span data-math=\"Y =\"></span> effective annual yield, <span data-math=\"r =\"></span> the interest rate in decimal form, and <span data-math=\"n =\"></span> the number of times the interest is compounded in a year. <span data-math=\"Y\"></span> is interpreted as the equivalent annual simple interest rate.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"Y = {\\left({1 + \\frac{{0.025}}{{365}}} \\right)^{365}} - 1 = 0.025314....\"></span></p>\n<p>Effective annual yield: 2.53%</p>\n<p>Earning 2.5% compounded daily gives you an effective annual yield of 2.53%, which is the equivalent of the annual simple interest rate.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The effective annual yield is 2.53%."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
